    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_73b26a0b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a historical photograph of Nazi leaders, including Adolf Hitler, standing before swastika flags. The overlaid text reads: 'when the americans pull up outside of auschwitz' and '*jew cooking time stops*'. This meme uses the horrific context of the Holocaust and the Nazi regime to create a grotesque, dehumanizing joke. It maps the arrival of American forces at Auschwitz (a site of mass murder) onto a stereotype that Jews are 'cooking' (implying they are being prepared for consumption), suggesting that their 'cooking time' stops when the Americans arrive. This is a direct and hateful attack on Jewish people, invoking the Holocaust as a punchline and reducing human suffering to a crude, racist joke. The meme is clearly intended to be offensive and harmful, relying on antisemitic tropes and the normalization of genocide as a comedic device. It is not merely humorous but propagates hate by trivializing the Holocaust and reinforcing dangerous stereotypes about Jewish people.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f23f7807"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
